sieve-filter-v2
; A test of the sieve-filter-v2 table form on the text line: comparisons, && || !, abs, min and
; max, if and else nested in for (and in each other), a choice parameter and the line's BASE.
; Neighbouring letters must be near each other in the alphabet (mode near: within gap), far from
; each other (far), or anything (any); a SPACE comes only after a letter, and a unit ends on a
; letter. Not shipped: CI checks the engine against the oracle with it.
id        toy-v2
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   lower27
describe  A toy of the v2 table form: neighbouring letters near, far or anything.
param     gap   int     2  0  26  how near is near
param     mode  choice  near near,far,any which neighbours pass

states    {BASE}
start     0
accept    1..{BASE - 1}
for x 0 {BASE - 1}
  for y 1 {max(1, min(BASE - 1, 99))}
    if {x == 0 || mode == 2}
      t {x} @{y} {y}
    else
      if {(mode == 0 && abs(x - y) <= gap) || (mode == 1 && !(abs(x - y) <= gap))}
        t {x} @{y} {y}
      fi
    fi
  done
  if {x != 0}
    t {x} @0 0
  fi
done
end
